% Microtones in the key signature, written with the shortcuts of the note
% syntax: K:G _/B _3/4e _3/4A comes from GitHub issue #10, where _/B
% stands for _1/2B.  process_microtones() (parseabc.c) read only the n/m
% and n forms, so _/B was ignored and B played natural.  Each bar played
% with the key signature is followed by the same bar with the microtones
% and accidentals written on the notes, which must play the same pitches
% with the same pitch bends: pitchof_b() (store.c) used to round the bend
% of a flat from the key signature one unit up.  A later K: field without
% a microtone for a note cancels it:
% setmap() (store.c) used to leave the microtone in force.
X:1
T:Microtones in the key signature
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:G _/B _3/4e _3/4A
B e A G|_/B _3/4e _3/4A G|
K:C ^/4F _//d
F d B e|^/4F _//d =B =e|
K:G
F d B A|^F =d =B =A|
